course: dictionary
lesson: 7331
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A plank is a long, flat piece of wood. Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the context to know which one the writer means. «Ruby built a den roof from old planks» tells you planks are pieces of wood, because she built a roof from them.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Hold your plank for thirty seconds» is about your body, not wood. Hold and seconds are the clues, and you can picture a body resting on its arms and toes, straight like a board.
explain: A plank can also be one main idea of a plan. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «the plank of the plan» still makes sense with the idea you chose, you have found the right meaning. If it does not, try the next one.
fact: A plank is a long, flat piece of wood.
fact: Plank can also mean an exercise where you hold your body straight, resting on your arms and toes.
fact: When a plank or beam bends under a load, its top is squashed and its bottom is stretched.
fact: The plural of plank is planks, which means more than one plank.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so context tells you which meaning is right.
exercise: «Ruby built a den roof from old planks.» What are planks here? | Holes dug in the ground | Strong ropes | * Long, flat pieces of wood | Tiny stones
exercise: In PE, the teacher says, «Hold your plank for thirty seconds.» What is a plank here? | Lying flat on the floor to rest | A type of bird | * An exercise where you hold your body straight on your arms and toes | A wooden toy boat
exercise: Ben says, «The main plank of my plan is a new park for everyone.» What does plank mean here? | A type of exercise | * One main idea of the plan | A piece of wood for the park | A ruler for measuring
test: Sam measured three planks before he cut them into equal pieces for a shelf. What is the plural of plank? | plank's | planking | planked | * planks
test: When a beam bends under a load, what happens to its bottom? | * It is stretched | It is squashed | It disappears | It turns into water
exam: Which sentence uses plank to mean one main idea of a plan? | The class built a plank of old wood for the bridge. | The pirate had to walk the plank. | Hold the plank until the timer rings. | * The plank of our plan was to keep the river clean.
